00000085491","entrez_id":["29957"],"uniprot":["Q6NUK1"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a carrier protein that transports ATP-Mg exchanging it for phosphate. Multiple transcript variants encoding different isoforms have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, May 2012].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6NUK1","text":"Electroneutral antiporter that mediates the transport of adenyl nucleotides through the inner mitochondrial membrane. Originally identified as an ATP-magnesium/inorganic phosphate antiporter, it also acts as a broad specificity adenyl nucleotide antiporter. By regulating the mitochondrial matrix adenyl nucleotide pool, could adapt to changing cellular energetic demands and indirectly regulate adenyl nucleotide-dependent metabolic pathways (PubMed:15123600, PubMed:22015608). In vitro, a low activity is also observed with guanyl and pyrimidine nucleotides (PubMed:15123600). May play a role in protecting cells against oxidative stress-induced cell death, by buffering calcium levels in the mitochondrial matrix through the formation of calcium-phosphate precipitates (PubMed:22015608, PubMed:29100093)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}